# {{ProjectName}}

A Struct microservice, scaffolded from the `standard` template: full
middleware chain, one example MVC vertical slice (`User`, in-memory
store), and the `struct` CLI.

## Running it

```bash
go build ./...
make run
# or: APP_ENV=development LOG_LEVEL=debug go run ./cmd/api
```

```bash
curl -X POST localhost:8080/v1/users \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"email":"you@example.com","password":"a-strong-password","locale":"en"}'

curl localhost:8080/v1/users/<id-from-above>
curl localhost:8080/healthz
```

## The `struct` CLI

```bash
go run ./cmd/struct doctor
go run ./cmd/struct routes
go run ./cmd/struct serve
```

This scaffold ships the Pass 1 command set (`serve`, `routes`, `health`,
`version`, `about`, `doctor`). The full framework's codegen commands
(`make model/controller/service/...`, `migrate`, `lint`) live in the
Struct framework repository's own `internal/app/codegen` and
`internal/app/cli` packages — copy those in if you want this project's
own `struct` binary to scaffold further code for itself.
